<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Cauci</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of Ireland's east coast recorded only in Ptolemy's 2nd-century Geography, whose name echoes the Chauci of northern Germany.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cauci are known solely from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150, which drew on earlier reports by merchants and sailors. He places them on the east coast of Ireland, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eblani">Eblani</a> to the north and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/manapii">Manapii</a> to the south, roughly in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wicklow">Wicklow</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers, settlements or way of life. Their name closely resembles that of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chauci">Chauci</a>, a Germanic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> coast, which has prompted speculation about settlers or traders from the Continent, but most scholars treat the likeness as coincidence or a copying error.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>No later source mentions them, and Irish tradition preserves no matching name. Their region later formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Kingdom of Leinster</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cauci.jpg" alt="Cauci" width="320" height="407"><figcaption>Image: Paul S · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_ire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=cauci" aria-label="Cauci on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4507 343 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cauci lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4827 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4827 599h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=cauci">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

